# extra-packages.txt — extra packages to bake into YOUR OpenCode image.
#
# Copy this file to `extra-packages.txt` (gitignored) and list one package per
# line. start.sh installs them at BUILD time on your host — which has normal
# internet, it does NOT go through the runtime Squid proxy — then bakes them
# into a thin LOCAL image layered on top of the pulled base. The locked-down
# runtime is unchanged: no new egress, no root for `dev`.
#
# Each line is one of:
#   NAME        an apt package (no prefix — backward compatible)
#   apt:NAME    an apt package (explicit, same as no prefix)
#   pip:SPEC    a pip requirement, e.g. pip:requests or pip:numpy==1.26.0
#
# apt packages are installed with `apt-get`; pip requirements with `pip3`
# (system-wide, so they land on the agent's PATH at runtime). pip packages
# auto-pull python3-pip if the base image doesn't already ship it.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are ignored. An empty or absent
# extra-packages.txt turns the feature off entirely (no extra build, current
# behaviour exactly).
#
# Examples (uncomment to use):
# cmake
# apt:ripgrep
# pip:requests
# pip:httpx==0.27.0
